{"kind":"report","text":"Approved: exact ui/message head 6d0bd190f3ce1129928c3678c5690cdbcc170bd2 on builder/ui-message-array-20261103, tree 0db11883, for source child 697bdbe2 under promise e9663ea8 and review request 57116142. This approval covers the content-block caller, its browser witness and the evidence. It claims no deployment, no repaired press in Goose, Claude or ChatGPT, and no Goose or G3b acceptance.\n\nScope. Main 81d25543 is an ancestor, the worktree is clean, and the branch is pushed. Against main, the head changes packages/mcp/browser/main.ts by one line, the generated views module, the fixture host, the browser case, the note and three manifests. The commit-message check passes for all three commits. Card paths change, so the head needs a Card run at its source: Card browser run 41741932669 succeeds at the frozen source 99617147, tree abe2db6c. From 99617147 to the head, only the note and two manifests change.\n\nWhat holds:\n\n- The defect is real. Goose 1.57.0 refused the press at params.content with \"expected array\", and both sealed upstream type snapshots declare content as a ContentBlock array. The note records that the prose example in the specification still shows an object.\n- main.ts is the only ui/message caller in the source tree. It now sends content:[{type:\"text\",text}] with the same text. The generated module carries the array in all four built copies and no object form.\n- The fixture host now refuses anything that is not a non-empty array of text blocks, with JSON-RPC -32602, and records the refusal. The case presses the generated production card, then asserts the exact params, no refusals, the exact chat text and one model turn.\n- The control reverts only the caller and rebuilds the bundle. The case then fails at the EXPLICIT HANDOFF CONTENT ARRAY assertion, with the object refused, zero chat messages and zero model turns. The driver restores main.ts to sha256 235d31f2… and generated.ts to b4a8d6b3…, and both match the head.\n\nThe gate passed. gate.exit at 99617147 reads exit 0, with the source clean before and after. Node ran 133, Counting 56, plain 3,607 with one skip and Native 1,070 with two skips. The PATH wrapper for mktemp changes only the temporary prefix, and the note says so.\n\nEvidence. The three manifests list 74 public files. All match their sizes and digests and are read-only, every SHA256SUMS file matches, and no unit holds an unlisted file. The scan for private keys, GitHub tokens and bearer values finds no match in the public files. The 38 selected private gate originals and all 2,274 files in the complete private inventory match their hashes and are read-only. The note names all three manifests' SHA-256 values.\n\nArchitecture: sound. The card follows the shared MCP Apps type, with no host-specific branch, and the strict fixture now enforces the same shape the hosts enforce.\n\nSecurity: no finding. The message text and the explicit press stay the same, and the change adds no tool, permission or data.\n\nSimplification: no required change. A limit for the live window: the fixture host is scripted, so this head proves no real host's behavior. Goose, Claude and ChatGPT each need one Ask in chat press after deployment. The archive owner passed in this gate, and parent 64552d40 stays open.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:01f7434daae8f4d0be83ed00a2e4baba89bcf4d4","binding":"assigned","head":"6d0bd190f3ce1129928c3678c5690cdbcc170bd2","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:49c83357ab40152587ff07ee7c9b6206d64cfefe\",\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:637390e1c6220d8470d9decf79ef0e176b41cfce\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:e9663ea89a3f76bf86f7068f559a9c17b2c257cb\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:637390e1c6220d8470d9decf79ef0e176b41cfce","review_path":"rev